        "original_id": "b0cada97-311b-5045-b97e-3a96b3f0c95e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Bossiaea, Ferraria, Platylobium\n- People: James Edward Smith, Wayne Cooper\n- Families: Fabaceae, Iridaceae\n- Places: Australia, tropical Africa, southern Africa\n- Topics: plant taxonomy, fashion design\n\nFacts:\n- Bossiaea is a genus in the pea family Fabaceae with about 70 species native to Australia.\n- Ferraria is a genus of monocotyledonous flowering plants in the family Iridaceae native to tropical and southern Africa.\n- James Edward Smith first described the genus Platylobium.\n- Platylobium is closely allied to Bossiaea within the Mirbelioids.\n- Wayne Cooper is a British-born fashion designer based in Australia.",
